From f086b453508624be9623b17bf7e6a6219d4bb50b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abian <BxiiDN@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:57:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Documentation, MAINTAINERS, components: drop references to
 arch/arm64/boot/uefi/

62e09f8 moved the loader's firmware (arch/arm64/boot/uefi/, arch/arm64/boot/u-boot/) to the companion
repository, but the documents, the LOADER entry of MAINTAINERS and the Mu-Silicium component still name
those paths, so tools_test (check-links) and maintainers_test fail on a clean checkout. Point the
documents at hakios-uefi, drop the MAINTAINERS pattern, and drop the Mu-Silicium pin whose file is gone.
The lint's old-name check (the HackiOS banner of a6d538c) is left as it is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Documentation/architecture.md | 4 ++--
 Documentation/porting.md      | 6 +++---
 MAINTAINERS                   | 1 -
 arch/arm64/boot/README.md     | 3 ++-
 components/upstream.dts       | 8 --------
 5 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/architecture.md b/Documentation/architecture.md
index 96a8795..f7f844d 100644
--- a/Documentation/architecture.md
+++ b/Documentation/architecture.md
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@ stock fastboot ──"fastboot boot"──► UEFI
 When the kernel is done, or panics, it returns to the loader, which still holds the phone's USB link.
 A reboot brings Android back.
 
-For the POCO X5 Pro's U-Boot path, see [the Redwood U-Boot build and console guide](../arch/arm64/boot/u-boot/README.md). U-Boot supplies the EFI environment and command shell; `loader.efi` still builds the XNU handoff.
+For the U-Boot path, see the companion firmware repository, [hakios-uefi](https://github.com/oosexgang/hakios-uefi), and its board porting guide. U-Boot supplies the EFI environment and command shell; `loader.efi` still builds the XNU handoff.
 
 ## Three layers, three kinds of change
 
@@ -181,7 +181,7 @@ against the scripts that fetch).
 | Darwin itself (IPSW contents) | Apple's files are never redistributed. | Extracted on your machine from Apple's IPSW. |
 | The phone's firmware (GPU, DSP, touch) | The vendor's; taken from the same phone it runs on. | `adb pull` from its Android. |
 | theos (cctools linker, iPhoneOS SDK) | A third-party toolchain. The kernel can be linked with LLVM's own Mach-O tools instead, with the SDK's headers alone ([building.md](building.md)); the `darwin/` scripts need theos. | [theos.dev](https://theos.dev/docs/installation-linux) |
-| The UEFI for a phone | A port of Mu-Silicium per device. | `arch/arm64/boot/uefi/` has the changes every port needs; a phone's own port is in its package. |
+| The UEFI for a phone | A port of Mu-Silicium per device, or U-Boot. | Kept outside this repository since the loader's companion repository was split off: [hakios-uefi](https://github.com/oosexgang/hakios-uefi) (U-Boot); a phone's own port is in its package. |
 | **Renoir's resident loader, its recovery payload tool and the user-space root tree** | They live in the team's working tree (`darwin-renoir`), which has not been published. | Not available yet. `darwin/tools/boot26.py` and the `darwin/userland/*.sh` scripts need it. |
 
 The last row is the gap between this repository and booting Renoir from a clean checkout.
diff --git a/Documentation/porting.md b/Documentation/porting.md
index 9d9fa52..96fc88b 100644
--- a/Documentation/porting.md
+++ b/Documentation/porting.md
@@ -88,9 +88,9 @@ Leave `features = <>;` (none) for now. Every key is explained in `arch/arm64/boo
 
 The loader runs under a UEFI. Port Mu-Silicium for the phone: the platform package with the phone's
 memory map, the UEFI drivers extracted from the phone's own firmware -- the first phone's package has a
-whole port under `arch/arm64/boot/uefi/` on the `devices` branch, with its README -- and what every port needs,
-in `arch/arm64/boot/uefi/` (`apply.sh PHONE_FILES` puts both into a clone): the two changes in
-`arch/arm64/boot/uefi/mu-silicium.patch`:
+whole port on the `devices` branch, with its README -- and what every port needs: the two changes below, which
+were kept in this repository until the loader's firmware moved to the companion
+repository [hakios-uefi](https://github.com/oosexgang/hakios-uefi) (which, as of this writing, carries the U-Boot path):
 
 - the boot shim copies the payload that follows the UEFI image to a reserved address;
 - the boot manager starts the loader from it instead of showing a menu.
